    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44330" root="&#xA;                        هلك&#xA;                    " body-key="h1">
                        
                            6
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهَالَكَ غَمًّا</span></b> 
                         [app. <i>He perished gradually by
reason of grief.</i>] (A, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سوس</span>: see 1 in that
art.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهَالَكَ عَلَيْهِ</span>
                        <i>He was vehemently eager for
it.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهَالَكَ فِيهِ</span>
                        <i>He strove, laboured,
toiled,</i> or <i>exerted himself, in it,</i> namely in
running; as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِهْتَلَكَ</span></b> . (TA.) <i>He strove,
laboured, toiled,</i> or <i>exerted himself, and
hastened, in it,</i> namely an affair; as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استهلك فيه</span></b> . (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَهَالَكَتْ</span> said of a
she-camel, <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشِقَتْ</span> [<i>She vehemently desired
the stallion</i>]. (AA, TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عشق</span>.)

